    "title": "World Cup qualifying results: Full 48-team field is set after playoffs",
    "text": "March 31, 2026Updated April 1, 2026, 3:48 p.m. ETAfter nearly three years of qualifiers, the 2026 World Cup field of 48 teams will be set with six winner-take-all matches on Tuesday to decide the final participants for this year's tournament.Four European berths were decided in the early evening Eastern time, with Turkey, Czechia, Sweden and Bosnia and Herzegovina grabbing the last of the 16 UEFA spots for the World Cup. The final two countries will be decided in FIFA’s intercontinental playoff finals: DR Congo vs Jamaica and Iraq vs. Bolivia, both being played in Mexico.The 2026 World Cup begins on June 11, with co-host Mexico facing South Africa in Mexico City. The winners of Tuesday's finals will slot into the World Cup groups assigned in December's draw.Keep up on results from around the globe on Tuesday: World Cup qualifying scores and schedule today UEFA playoff finalsBosnia and Herzegovina 1, Italy 1 – BOSNIA WINS 4-1 ON PENALTIESSweden 3, Poland 2Czechia 2, Denmark 2 – CZECHIA WINS 3-1 ON PENALTIESTurkey 1, Kosovo 0Watch World Cup qualifying playoffs on Fubo Intercontinental playoff finalsDR Congo 1, Jamaica 0Iraq 2, Bolivia 1 World Cup qualifying group resultsCzechia joins Group A: Mexico, South Africa and South Korea.Bosnia and Herzegovina joins Group B: Canada, Qatar and Switzerland.Turkey joins Group D: United States, Paraguay and Australia.Sweden joins Group F: Netherlands, Japan and Tunisia.Iraq joins Group I: France, Senegal and Norway.DR Congo joins Group K: Portugal, Uzbekistan and Colombia.Teams qualified for 2026 World CupUpdated 1:13 p.m. ET, Wednesday with 48/48 places bookedHost nations: Canada, Mexico, United StatesAsia: Australia, Iran, Japan, Jordan, Qatar, Saudi Arabia, South Korea, Uzbekistan, *IraqAfrica: Algeria, Cape Verde, DR Congo, Egypt, Ghana, Ivory Coast, Morocco, Senegal, South Africa, TunisiaConcacaf: Curaçao, Haiti, PanamaEurope: Austria, Belgium, Bosnia and Herzegovina, Croatia, Czechia, England, France, Germany, 